${NRCELL_3_ID}        3
${ue_1_id}            1

*** Keywords ***

TC 1227 UPD009 Counters Test
    [Documentation]        verification of PM counters of 1227-A-UPD009
    [Arguments]            ${params}        ${Vendor_Param}
    Set Suite Variable     ${params}
    Init Sequence          ${params}
    Step                   Set RAD Params Of 1227       
    Step                   Config1227.Vendor File Config With Specific Settings     argument=${Vendor_Param}
    Step                   Config1227.Update 1227 Params in OAM SCF    
    Critical Step          Restart TL
    Step                   Multi Cells Setup SA 1227                  argument=${params.nbCell}
    # Step                   SA Call of 1 UE
    Step                   SA Call With UE Id   argument=${ue_1_id}
    Step                   Activate Sherpa On All Cells
    Step                   Wait In Seconds
    Step                   Stop Sherpa Collection
    Step                   sleep     argument=720s
    Step                   Collect All Current PM Counters Files
    Step                   Set 1227 PM Counters ID Variables
    Step                   Check UPD009 PM Counters         argument=${NRCELL_1_ID}
    Step                   Check BB Pooling PM Counters     argument=${NRCELL_1_ID}
    Step                   Check BB Pooling PM Counters     argument=${NRCELL_3_ID}
    

Set 1227 PM Counters ID Variables
    [Documentation]                 1227 PM Counters List :
    ...                             PM Counters of UPD009
    ...                              PM Counter ID            PM Counter Description
    ...                              M55308C00005             Data slot with PDSCH
    ...                              M55308C00015             SS Burst slot with PDSCH
    ...                              M55308C00017             TRS Slot with PDSCH
    ...                              M55308C03001             PDSCH OFDM symbols
    ...                              M55308C03005             PDSCH OFDM symbols Time
    ...                              M55308C10003             PRBs available for PDSCH 
    ...                              M55308C10001             PRBs used for PDSCH   
    ${PM_Data_Slot_PDSCH}              Set Variable         M55308C00005
    ${PM_SSB_Slot_PDSCH}               Set Variable         M55308C00015
    ${PM_TRS_Slot_PDSCH}               Set Variable         M55308C00017
    ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols}           Set Variable         M55308C03001
    ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols_Time}      Set Variable         M55308C03005
    ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH}              Set Variable         M55308C10003
    ${PM_PRB_Used_PDSCH}               Set Variable         M55308C10001
    ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}      Set Variable         M55308C10005
    ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}      Set Variable         M55308C10006
    Set Suite Variable                 ${PM_Data_Slot_PDSCH}
    Set Suite Variable                 ${PM_SSB_Slot_PDSCH}
    Set Suite Variable                 ${PM_TRS_Slot_PDSCH} 
    Set Suite Variable                 ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols}
    Set Suite Variable                 ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols_Time} 
    Set Suite Variable                 ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH}
    Set Suite Variable                 ${PM_PRB_Used_PDSCH}
    Set Suite Variable                 ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool} 
    Set Suite Variable                 ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}

Set 1227 E DSS Counters ID Variables
    [Documentation]                 1227 E DSS PM Counters List :
    ...                              PM Counter ID            PM Counter Description
    ...                              M55332C00001             Number of Data slot assigned to NR
    ...                              M55332C01001             Number of UL PRBs assigned to NR
    ...                              M55332C02001             Total number of available DL Slots
    ...                              M55332C02002             Total number of available UL PRBs
    ${DL_Slots_NR}                   Set Variable               M55332C00001       
    ${UL_PRB_NR}                     Set Variable               M55332C01001
    ${DL_Slots_Total}                Set Variable               M55332C02001
    ${UL_PRB_Total}                  Set Variable               M55332C02002
    Set Suite Variable               ${DL_Slots_NR} 
    Set Suite Variable               ${UL_PRB_NR}
    Set Suite Variable               ${DL_Slots_Total} 
    Set Suite Variable               ${UL_PRB_Total}

Collect All Current PM Counters Files
    [Documentation]                 KW to get counters and store in specific directory with day date
    ${date}                         Get Current Date
    ${date_in_dir_name}             Convert Date         ${date}     result_format=%d%m%Y_%H%M
    ${log_path_pm}                  Set Variable         ${LOG_PATH}/PM_${date_in_dir_name}  
    BuiltIn.Log                     The PM counters file collected from gnb will be stored under : ${log_path_pm}
    ${pm_latest}                    Counters.Collect PM files from BTS    ${log_path_pm}
    set Suite Variable              ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${pm_latest}
    set Suite Variable              ${log_path_pm}
    BuiltIn.Log                     Latest pm counters file : ${LATEST_PM_FILE}


Check UPD009 PM Counters
    [Documentation]                 1) To Check PRB Allocation on DL PDSCH Slots:
    ...                               M55308C10001=Total numbers of PRBs Used for PDSCH in 5 mins' interval;
    ...                               M55308C00005=Total Data slots with PDSCH cumulated in 5mins' interval;
    ...                               M55308C00015=Total SSB slots with PDSCH cumulated in 5mins' interval;
    ...                               M55308C00017=Total TRS slots with PDSCH cumulated in 5mins' interval;
    ...                               M55308C10001/(M55308C00005+M55308C00015+M55308C00017)=Num of PRB allocated on each PDSCH slot
    ...                               should be greater than 0 and <= 104 
    ...                               (Since in RR Algo, selected Cell Max PRB=106, notSelected Cell Max PRB=101, so
    ...                               in average, the MaxPRB would be less than (106+101)/2 ) 
    ...                             2)To Check that : 
    ...                               M55308C03001=total PDSCH OFDM symbols allocated during 5mins' interval
    ...                               M55308C03005=total Time duration of PDSCH OFDM symbols allocated during 5 mins' interval
    ...                               M55308C03005/M55308C03001 should be 71,4 micro sec (time duration of one symbol in FR1 FDD30khz)
    ...                             3)To Check that : 
    ...                               M55308C03001/(M55308C00005+M55308C00015+M55308C00017) <=13 symbols per pdsch grant  
    [Arguments]                     ${NRCELL_ID} 
    Dated Log                       ============================================================================
    Dated Log                         ${PM_PRB_Used_PDSCH} : Total numbers of PRBs Used for PDSCH in 5 mins' interval
    Dated Log                       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ${Value_PM_PRB_Used_PDSCH}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_PRB_Used_PDSCH}       ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of PRB used for PDSCH: ${PM_PRB_Used_PDSCH} : ${Value_PM_PRB_Used_PDSCH}
    ${Value_PM_Data_Slot_PDSCH}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_Data_Slot_PDSCH}      ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of Data Slot PDSCH: ${PM_Data_Slot_PDSCH} : ${Value_PM_Data_Slot_PDSCH}
    ${Value_PM_SSB_Slot_PDSCH}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_SSB_Slot_PDSCH}     ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of SSB Slot PDSCH : ${PM_SSB_Slot_PDSCH} : ${Value_PM_SSB_Slot_PDSCH}
    ${Value_PM_TRS_Slot_PDSCH}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_TRS_Slot_PDSCH}    ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of TRS Slot PDSCH: ${PM_TRS_Slot_PDSCH} : ${Value_PM_TRS_Slot_PDSCH}
    ${Value_PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols}=         Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                     ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols}       ${NRCELL_ID} 
    Dated Log                         Value of Total PDSCH OFDM Symbols: ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols} : ${Value_PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols}
    ${Value_PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols_Time}=    Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                     ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols_Time}       ${NRCELL_ID}   
    Dated Log                         Value of Total PDSCH Symbols Time: ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols_Time} : ${Value_PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols_Time}
    ${Sum_Pdsch_Slots}=                 Evaluate  ${Value_PM_Data_Slot_PDSCH}+${Value_PM_SSB_Slot_PDSCH}+${Value_PM_TRS_Slot_PDSCH}
    ${Num_PRB_Per_Slot}=                Evaluate  int(${Value_PM_PRB_Used_PDSCH}/${Sum_Pdsch_Slots})
    ${Num_Symbol_Per_Slot}=             Evaluate  int(${Value_PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols}/${Sum_Pdsch_Slots})
    ${Time_Duration_Per_Symbol}=        Evaluate  int(${Value_PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols_Time}/${Value_PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols})
    Dated Log                           Value of : ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols_Time} divised by ${PM_PDSCH_OFDM_Symbols}: ${Time_Duration_Per_Symbol}
    Dated Log                           Num of PRB Per slot : ${Num_PRB_Per_Slot}
    Dated Log                           Num of symbols per Pdsch slot : ${Num_Symbol_Per_Slot}
    should be true    0 < ${Num_PRB_Per_Slot} <= 104
    should be true    0 < ${Num_Symbol_Per_Slot} <= 13
    should be true    ${Time_Duration_Per_Symbol}==71



Check BB Pooling PM Counters
    [Documentation]                 1) To Check total PRB Available on PDSCH & PUSCH when 1227 activated 
    ...                               M55308C10005=Total number of PRBs Available for PDSCH in 5 mins' interval;
    ...                               M55308C10006=Total number of PRBs Available for PUSCH in 5 mins' interval; 
    ...                             The calculation details of the expected values is documented in squad 41 technical oneNote
    [Arguments]                     ${NRCELL_ID}  
    Dated Log                       ============================================================================
    Dated Log                         ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool} : Total number of PRBs Available for PDSCH in 5 mins' interval;
    ...                               ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool} : Total number of PRBs Available for PUSCH in 5 mins' interval;
    Dated Log                       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ${Value_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}       ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of PRB used for PDSCH: ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool} : ${Value_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}
    ${Value_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}      ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of PRB used for PUSCH: ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool} : ${Value_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}
    ${Num_PRB_PDSCH_Per_Slot}         Evaluate  int(${Value_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}/300000)
    ${Num_PRB_PUSCH_Per_Slot}         Evaluate  int(${Value_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}/300000)
    # should be true      ${Num_PRB_PDSCH_Per_Slot}==103
    should be true      ${Num_PRB_PDSCH_Per_Slot}==96
    # should be true      ${Num_PRB_PUSCH_Per_Slot}==51
    should be true      ${Num_PRB_PUSCH_Per_Slot}==45

Verify 1227 E Load Based Pooling PM counters
    [Documentation]                 1) To Check total PRB Available on PDSCH & PUSCH when 1227 activated 
    ...                               M55308C10005=Total number of PRBs Available for PDSCH in 5 mins' interval;
    ...                               M55308C10006=Total number of PRBs Available for PUSCH in 5 mins' interval;
    ...				      Cell1 & Cell2 share the same L1Subpool	
    ...                               Cell 2 : PRBs available for PDSCH with L1 baseband pooling activated (M55308C10005) = X2
    ...                               Cell 2 : PRBs available for PUSCH with L1 baseband pooling activated (M55308C10006) = Y2
    ...                               Cell 1 : PRBs available for PDSCH with L1 baseband pooling activated (M55308C10005) = X1
    ...                               Cell 1 : PRBs available for PUSCH with L1 baseband pooling activated (M55308C10006) = Y1
    ...                               For DL : (X1+X3)/300000 should be around 185 PRB per slot; X2 > X1
    ...                               For UL : (Y1+Y3)/300000 should be around 85 PRB per slot;  Y2 > Y1
    # ${NRCELL_1_ID}          Set Variable        1
    # ${NRCELL_3_ID}          Set Variable        3
    ${expected_PDSCH_PRB}   Set Variable        185
    ${expected_PUSCH_PRB}   Set Variable        85   
    # Retrieve the counters' value of CELL 2
    Dated Log                       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ${Value_1_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}       ${NRCELL_2_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of Cell 2 PRB used for PDSCH: ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool} : ${Value_1_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}
    ${Value_1_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}      ${NRCELL_2_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of Cell 2 PRB used for PUSCH: ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool} : ${Value_1_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}
    # Retrieve the counters' value of CELL 1
    Dated Log                       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ${Value_2_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}       ${NRCELL_1_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of Cell 1 PRB used for PDSCH: ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool} : ${Value_2_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}
    ${Value_2_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}=             Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}      ${NRCELL_1_ID}
    Dated Log                         Value of Cell 1 PRB used for PUSCH: ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool} : ${Value_2_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}
    # Verify the values 
    ${Num_PRB_PDSCH_Per_Slot}         Evaluate  int((${Value_1_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}+${Value_2_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool})/300000)
    ${Num_PRB_PUSCH_Per_Slot}         Evaluate  int((${Value_1_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}+${Value_2_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool})/300000)
    should be true      ${Value_1_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool} > ${Value_2_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool}
    should be true      ${Value_2_PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool} > ${Value_2_PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool}
    should be true      ${Num_PRB_PDSCH_Per_Slot}==${expected_PDSCH_PRB}
    should be true      ${Num_PRB_PUSCH_Per_Slot}==${expected_PUSCH_PRB}

Verify 1227 E LoadBased DSS counters
    [Documentation]             To verify with 1227 E DSS activated, Load based Pooling, the DSS counters : 
    ...                         	Number of DL Slots assigned to NR (M55332C00001) = X
	...                             Number of UL PRBs assigned to NR (M55332C01001) = Y
	...                             Total number of available DL Slots (M55332C02001) = Z
	...                             Total number of available UL PRBs (M55332C02002) = W
    ...                     	For DL : 
	...                         The value of M55332C00001 (X) should be about :   X= 300000*70% = 210000    300000*95%=285000 
	...                         The value of M55332C02001 (Z) should be about :   300000*(1-2/80) = 292500   (300000*(1-2/40)=285000 
	...                         (Note :   as per 1227-E UPD 10,  2 slots over 40 no PDSCH) 
	...                     	For UL : 
	...                         The value of M55332C01001 (Y) divided by M55332C02002 (W) :  Y/W = 70/106 = 0,6604 
	...                         (Note : 70 is the number of PUSCH PRB allocated to NR sent in egate command during the ressource allocation)
    [Arguments]                 ${NRCELL_ID} 
    Dated Log                   ============================================================================
    Dated Log                   ${DL_Slots_NR} : Number of DL Slots Assigned to NR
    Dated Log                   ${UL_PRB_NR} : Number of UL PRBs assigned to NR 
    Dated Log                   ${DL_Slots_Total} : Number of available DL Slots 
    Dated Log                   ${UL_PRB_Total} : Total number of available UL PRBs
    Dated Log                   ============================================================================
    ${Value_DL_Slots_NR}=       Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${DL_Slots_NR}       ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                   Value of ${DL_Slots_NR} : ${Value_DL_Slots_NR}
    ${Value_UL_PRB_NR}=         Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${UL_PRB_NR}       ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                   Value of ${UL_PRB_NR} : ${Value_UL_PRB_NR}
    ${Value_DL_Slots_Total}=    Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${DL_Slots_Total}       ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                   Value of ${DL_Slots_Total} : ${Value_DL_Slots_Total}
    ${Value_UL_PRB_Total}=       Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${UL_PRB_Total}       ${NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                   Value of ${UL_PRB_Total} : ${Value_UL_PRB_Total}
    # check values 
    # ${expected_DL_Slots_NR}=    Evaluate    300000*0.95
    # should be true              ${Value_DL_Slots_NR} >= ${expected_DL_Slots_NR}
    ${expected_DL_Slots_Total}=     Evaluate    300000*(1-2/40)
    should be true                  ${Value_DL_Slots_Total} >= ${expected_DL_Slots_Total}
    should be true                  ${Value_DL_Slots_Total}*0.9 <= ${Value_DL_Slots_NR} <= ${Value_DL_Slots_Total}
    ${expected_UL_PRB_ratio_NR}=    Evaluate    0.66
    ${actual_UL_PRB_ratio_NR}=      Evaluate    ${Value_UL_PRB_NR}/${Value_UL_PRB_Total}
    should be true                  ${actual_UL_PRB_ratio_NR} >= ${expected_UL_PRB_ratio_NR}


Verify 1227 E LoadBased DSS counters By CellID And Ratio Expected
    [Documentation]             To verify with 1227 E DSS activated, Load based Pooling, the DSS counters : 
    ...                         	Number of DL Slots assigned to NR (M55332C00001) = X
	...                             Number of UL PRBs assigned to NR (M55332C01001) = Y
	...                             Total number of available DL Slots (M55332C02001) = Z
	...                             Total number of available UL PRBs (M55332C02002) = W
    ...                           For a given CellID, check the value of counters are the same as expected (+/-0.01)
    ...                     	  For DL : X/Z=DL Dss ratio
	...                             The value of M55332C00001 (X) / The value of M55332C02001 (Z) should be the DL Dss ratio
	...                     	  For UL : Y/W=UL PRB ratio 
	...                             The value of M55332C01001 (Y) divided by M55332C02002 (W) :  Y/W = 70/106 = 0,6604 
	...                             (Note : 70 is the number of PUSCH PRB allocated to NR sent in egate command during the ressource allocation)
    ...                         To use this keyword: 
    ...                           1) first define a dictionary with the following structure : 
    ...                            &{DSS_Counter_Expectation}       NRCELL_ID=1     DL_Ratio_Expected=0.70       UL_Ratio_Expected=0.70
    
    [Arguments]                 ${DSS_Counter_Expectation} 
    Dated Log                   ============================================================================
    Dated Log                   ${DL_Slots_NR} : Number of DL Slots Assigned to NR
    Dated Log                   ${UL_PRB_NR} : Number of UL PRBs assigned to NR 
    Dated Log                   ${DL_Slots_Total} : Number of available DL Slots 
    Dated Log                   ${UL_PRB_Total} : Total number of available UL PRBs
    Dated Log                   ============================================================================
    ${Value_DL_Slots_NR}=       Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${DL_Slots_NR}       ${DSS_Counter_Expectation.NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                   Value of ${DL_Slots_NR} : ${Value_DL_Slots_NR}
    ${Value_UL_PRB_NR}=         Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${UL_PRB_NR}       ${DSS_Counter_Expectation.NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                   Value of ${UL_PRB_NR} : ${Value_UL_PRB_NR}
    ${Value_DL_Slots_Total}=    Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${DL_Slots_Total}       ${DSS_Counter_Expectation.NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                   Value of ${DL_Slots_Total} : ${Value_DL_Slots_Total}
    ${Value_UL_PRB_Total}=       Counters.Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID     
    ...                                    ${LATEST_PM_FILE}       ${UL_PRB_Total}       ${DSS_Counter_Expectation.NRCELL_ID}
    Dated Log                   Value of ${UL_PRB_Total} : ${Value_UL_PRB_Total}
   
    # ${expected_DL_Slots_Total}=     Evaluate    300000*(1-2/40)
    # should be true                  ${Value_DL_Slots_Total} >= ${expected_DL_Slots_Total}
    # should be true                  ${Value_DL_Slots_Total}*0.9 <= ${Value_DL_Slots_NR} <= ${Value_DL_Slots_Total}
    # ${expected_UL_PRB_ratio_NR}=    Evaluate    0.66
    ${actual_UL_PRB_ratio_NR}=      Evaluate    ${Value_UL_PRB_NR}/${Value_UL_PRB_Total}
    should be true                  ${actual_UL_PRB_ratio_NR} >= ${DSS_Counter_Expectation.UL_Ratio_Expected} 
    ${actual_DL_Ratio_NR}=          Evaluate    ${Value_DL_Slots_NR}/${Value_DL_Slots_Total} 
    ${Ratio_Expected}               Set Variable     ${DSS_Counter_Expectation.DL_Ratio_Expected}
    should be true                  ${Ratio_Expected}-0.01 <= ${actual_DL_Ratio_NR} <= ${Ratio_Expected}+0.01              


Check BB Pooling PM Counters By CellID And Expected values
    [Documentation]                 1) To Check total PRB Available on PDSCH & PUSCH when 1227 activated 
    ...                               M55308C10005 (X)=Total number of PRBs Available for PDSCH in 5 mins' interval;
    ...                               M55308C10006 (Y) =Total number of PRBs Available for PUSCH in 5 mins' interval;   
    ...                             Check for the given Cell ID, the num. of PRB DL & UL per slot are as expected (depending on Test Condition)
    ...                                   DL :  X/300000 = 103 (round robin, average PRB 20Mhz DL)
    ...                                   UL :  Y/300000 = 51  (round robin, average PRB 20Mhz UL)
    ...                             To use the keyword : 
    ...                                 - define a variable of type Dictionary which has the following structure : 
    ...                                   eg.  &{Pooling_Counters_Expected_1}    
    ...                                             NRCELL_ID=1    
    ...                                             PDSCH_PRB_Expected=106      
    ...                                             PUSCH_PRB_Expected=106
    ...                                 - then call the kw with the variable like this : 
    ...                                     Check BB Pooling PM Counters By CellID And Expected values    ${Pooling_Counters_Expected_1}
    [Arguments]                     ${Pooling_Counters_Expected} 
    Dated Log                       =======================================================================
    Dated Log                       Cell ${Pooling_Counters_Expected.NRCELL_ID} : 
    Dated Log                         ${PM_PRB_Avail_PDSCH_BB_Pool} : Total number of PRBs Available for PDSCH in 5 mins' interval;
    Dated Log                         ${PM_PRB_Avail_PUSCH_BB_Pool} : Total number of PRBs Available for PUSCH in 5 mins' interval;
    Dated Log                       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
